# Power operated vehicle, Group 1 (K0800, K0801, K0802), from Medicare LCD L33789 (the DME MACs). Status draft:
# awaiting clinical sign-off (vaglio signoff). Every clause is quoted from library/sources/L33789-power-mobility.txt,
# which lists the codes itself.
#
# Drafted by hand. The LCD's basic criteria A to C (a mobility limitation that significantly impairs mobility-related
# activities of daily living in the home; a cane or walker cannot resolve it; not enough upper extremity function to
# self-propel an optimally configured manual wheelchair), then the POV criteria D to I: able to transfer, steer with the
# tiller and stay stable; the mental and physical capability for safe use; a home that allows it; the beneficiary's
# weight within the device's class; it will significantly improve MRADLs and be used in the home; and no unwillingness
# to use it. All are required. Questions only: the LCD names no codes for any of them. Group 2 POVs (K0806-K0808) the
# LCD denies outright, power wheelchairs have their own criteria: neither is decided here. The order, the face-to-face
# examination and the home assessment are the documentation the policy article and the standard documentation article
# require; the reviewer reads those. The DME MACs' LCD is the same in every jurisdiction, so no states are named.
policy pov
  title "Power operated vehicle, Group 1 (K0800-K0802)"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Medicare LCD L33789, Power Mobility Devices (DME MACs): basic coverage criteria and power operated vehicles"
  status draft
  authority lcd
  lines medicare-advantage medicare
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/pov
  service hcpcs K0800 K0801 K0802

evidence mobility_limitation
  text "A mobility limitation that significantly impairs mobility-related activities of daily living (toileting, feeding, dressing, grooming, bathing) in the home"
  clause "The beneficiary has a mobility limitation that significantly impairs his/her ability to participate in one or more mobility-related activities of daily living (MRADLs) such as toileting, feeding, dressing, grooming, and bathing in customary locations in the home."
  find question mobility-limitation
  request document loinc 11488-4

evidence cane_walker_insufficient
  text "A fitted cane or walker cannot sufficiently and safely resolve the limitation"
  clause "The beneficiary’s mobility limitation cannot be sufficiently and safely resolved by the use of an appropriately fitted cane or walker."
  find question cane-walker-insufficient

evidence manual_chair_insufficient
  text "Not enough upper extremity function to self-propel an optimally configured manual wheelchair in the home"
  clause "The beneficiary does not have sufficient upper extremity function to self-propel an optimally-configured manual wheelchair in the home to perform MRADLs during a typical day."
  find question manual-chair-insufficient

evidence can_operate
  text "Able to transfer safely, operate the tiller and stay posturally stable on a POV in the home"
  clause "Maintain postural stability and position while operating the POV in the home."
  find question can-operate-pov

evidence capable
  text "Mental and physical capabilities sufficient for safe use of a POV in the home"
  clause "The beneficiary’s mental capabilities (e.g., cognition, judgment) and physical capabilities (e.g., vision) are sufficient for safe mobility using a POV in the home."
  find question capable

evidence home_suitable
  text "The home allows access between rooms, maneuvering space and surfaces for the POV"
  clause "The beneficiary’s home provides adequate access between rooms, maneuvering space, and surfaces for the operation of the POV that is provided."
  find question home-suitable

evidence weight_in_class
  text "The beneficiary's weight is within the weight class of the POV provided"
  clause "The beneficiary’s weight is less than or equal to the weight capacity of the POV that is provided and greater than or equal to 95% of the weight capacity of the next lower weight class POV"
  find question weight-in-class

evidence will_improve
  text "The POV will significantly improve participation in MRADLs, and will be used in the home"
  clause "Use of a POV will significantly improve the beneficiary’s ability to participate in MRADLs and the beneficiary will use it in the home."
  find question will-improve

evidence unwilling
  text "The beneficiary has expressed unwillingness to use a POV in the home"
  clause "The beneficiary has not expressed an unwillingness to use a POV in the home."
  find question unwilling

criterion no_limitation
  text "A mobility limitation impairing MRADLs in the home is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary has a mobility limitation that significantly impairs his/her ability to participate in one or more mobility-related activities of daily living (MRADLs) such as toileting, feeding, dressing, grooming, and bathing in customary locations in the home."
  defeated by mobility_limitation

criterion cane_walker_unshown
  text "That a cane or walker cannot resolve it is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary’s mobility limitation cannot be sufficiently and safely resolved by the use of an appropriately fitted cane or walker."
  defeated by cane_walker_insufficient

criterion manual_chair_unshown
  text "That a manual wheelchair cannot be self-propelled is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary does not have sufficient upper extremity function to self-propel an optimally-configured manual wheelchair in the home to perform MRADLs during a typical day."
  defeated by manual_chair_insufficient

criterion operation_unshown
  text "Safe transfer, tiller steering and postural stability are not documented."
  clause "Maintain postural stability and position while operating the POV in the home."
  defeated by can_operate

criterion capability_unshown
  text "Sufficient mental and physical capability for safe use is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary’s mental capabilities (e.g., cognition, judgment) and physical capabilities (e.g., vision) are sufficient for safe mobility using a POV in the home."
  defeated by capable

criterion home_unshown
  text "A home that allows the POV is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary’s home provides adequate access between rooms, maneuvering space, and surfaces for the operation of the POV that is provided."
  defeated by home_suitable

criterion weight_unshown
  text "A weight within the POV's class is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary’s weight is less than or equal to the weight capacity of the POV that is provided and greater than or equal to 95% of the weight capacity of the next lower weight class POV"
  defeated by weight_in_class

criterion improvement_unshown
  text "Significant improvement in MRADLs, with use in the home, is not documented."
  clause "Use of a POV will significantly improve the beneficiary’s ability to participate in MRADLs and the beneficiary will use it in the home."
  defeated by will_improve

criterion criteria_met
  text "Basic criteria A to C and POV criteria D to H are met."
  clause "A POV is covered if all of the basic coverage criteria (A-C) have been met and if criteria D-I are also met."
  defeated by no_limitation cane_walker_unshown manual_chair_unshown operation_unshown capability_unshown home_unshown weight_unshown improvement_unshown

criterion willing
  text "No unwillingness to use the POV in the home has been expressed."
  clause "The beneficiary has not expressed an unwillingness to use a POV in the home."
  defeated by unwilling

decision approve approves
  text "Approve the power operated vehicle."
  clause "A POV is covered if all of the basic coverage criteria (A-C) have been met and if criteria D-I are also met."
  defeated by no_limitation cane_walker_unshown manual_chair_unshown operation_unshown capability_unshown home_unshown weight_unshown improvement_unshown unwilling

decision deny_criteria denies
  text "Deny: a basic or POV coverage criterion is not met."
  clause "If a POV will be used inside the home and coverage criteria A-I are not met, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by criteria_met

decision deny_unwilling denies
  text "Deny: the beneficiary has expressed unwillingness to use a POV in the home."
  clause "If a POV will be used inside the home and coverage criteria A-I are not met, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by willing
